.TH TRUE "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
true \- do nothing, successfully
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
[\fI\,ignored command line arguments\/\fR]
.br
.B true
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Exit with a status code indicating success.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/true#true--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/true#true--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.PP
Your shell may have its own version of true, which usually supersedes
the version described here.  Please refer to your shell's documentation
for details about the options it supports.
